    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, just finished a rumenotomy on one of my heifers. need a protocol for the next few days to make sure she recovers okay. specifically what should i be looking for regarding infection and when can i start bringing her back onto feed? thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Post-rumenotomy care is crucial for a smooth recovery. Closely monitor the incision site daily for any signs of infection, such as excessive swelling, redness, foul odor, or discharge. Regarding feeding, you should start offering small, easily digestible rations gradually, once the initial acute recovery phase has passed and the incision appears stable. Always keep her comfortable and manage her stress levels throughout this healing period.",
      "source": "target",
